    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start, but it sounds a bit like a standard talking point. i need more substance. specifically, how do we poke holes in their argument about \"wealth redistribution as a matter of justice\"? they always pivot to morality when we talk about economics. what's the most effective way to frame that as being logically unsound or even hypocritical?",
